## Data Retrieval

Data retrieval is the first step in any bioinformatics workflow, involving the collection of reliable biological data from publicly
available databases. In this project, biological sequences and structural information were obtained from databases such as NCBI, UniProt,
and the Protein Data Bank (PDB). NCBI was used to retrieve nucleotide and protein sequences, UniProt provided curated protein sequences and
functional annotations, and PDB supplied experimentally determined three-dimensional protein structures. The retrieved data served as the
foundation for subsequent analyses, including sequence alignment, protein characterization, structure prediction, validation, and
phylogenetic analysis.

